From 5fa17f4cfdefb1c441c222b772e59a0ab08f2212 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:38:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] explain same-label pool backlog before
 capability-dropping moves

A ready pool card's origin cannot lease its labels, but that does not mean
no worker can. The prior notice omitted same-label queue evidence and
recommended re-placement. That prompted removal of hub-write from work
that later needed it. The local mismatch was mistaken for a fleet fault
because the notice never connected recent matching worker claims with
the waiting card's label set.

Add approximate same-label predecessors using canonical dispatch order
and distinct Board-holder claims in the last 30 minutes. Require exact
labels, a currently available matching machine and no later move/edit;
exclude ambiguous claims instead of treating current labels as history.
Report board-view scope and no pickup-time guarantee. Preserve prior
board/count/clock fixes and existing held/draining semantics.

Refuse a ready card's capability-dropping move when usable recent claims
contradict placement failure. Explicit force retains existing gates and
records the capacity evidence in the moved audit event.

Proof: the unchanged notice/move regression fails twice on base callers
(missing queue count; capability drop accepted). With the patch, 21 new
tests and 26 prior board/count/clock tests pass. Broader consumer suites,
mutation coverage, live-row replay and shipping gates remain to verify.
Task: t_01a1d6ec84eb29dc; lineage: t_01a1ce30a39b7172.
